# Binary files, marked explicitly.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. core.autocrlf is true on the Windows checkouts, and
# with no .gitattributes git decides text-versus-binary by a content heuristic.
# It got that wrong for out/nonparental_rate_by_state_2019.png: it applied
# LF-to-CRLF conversion on checkout and produced a 152,224-byte working file
# that could never match the 113,814-byte blob, so the file showed as modified
# forever and `git checkout --` re-applied the corruption instead of fixing it.
#
# The heuristic happens to read the PDFs and the Stata files correctly today.
# It is still a heuristic. Naming the extensions costs nothing and does not
# depend on file content.
#
# NOTE: deliberately no `* text=auto`. That would renormalise line endings
# across every tracked text file in one commit, which is a much larger change
# than this problem warrants.

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.dta   binary
*.sas7bdat binary
*.rds   binary
*.RData binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.xlsm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.parquet binary

# Archived source snapshots -- preserve bytes for SHA-256 registry.
# Publisher whitespace retained; compare replacements via registered hashes.
state_data/raw/** binary
resources/licensing/US_ICPSR37700__center_and_home_child_staff_ratios_by_age__2017.csv -text
